    "details": "<p><strong>Introduction:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>HackKro</strong>&nbsp;is organizing&nbsp;<strong>CodeClash 1.0</strong>, a competitive coding event hosted on the Unstop platform. The objective of this event is to provide students with a nationwide platform to showcase their problem-solving skills, enhance logical thinking, and compete with top coding talent. Whether you are a beginner or an experienced developer, CodeClash 1.0 is designed to test your limits and boost your technical growth.</p>\n<p><strong>Event Details:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Event Name:</strong>&nbsp;CodeClash 1.0</li>\n<li><strong>Organized By:</strong>&nbsp;HackKro</li>\n<li><strong>Date:</strong> 25th September 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Mode:</strong>&nbsp;Online (via Unstop)</li>\n<li><strong>Eligibility:</strong>&nbsp;Open to all college students across all streams and years</li>\n<li><strong>Registration Fee:</strong>&nbsp;Free</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rewards &amp; Certificates:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Winner Certificate:</strong>&nbsp;Awarded to top performers</li>\n<li><strong>Participation Certificate:</strong>&nbsp;Provided to all active participants</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Structure &amp; Rounds:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;Coding Challenge</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Date &amp; Time:</strong> 25th September 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong>&nbsp;30 Minutes</li>\n<li><strong>Format:</strong>&nbsp;30 Multiple Choice Questions</li>\n<li><strong>Topics:</strong>&nbsp;Core Programming (C++, Java, Python), Data Structures Basics, Aptitude &amp; Logical Reasoning</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility Criteria:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to undergraduate and postgraduate college students.</li>\n<li>Participants must register individually using a valid email ID.</li>\n<li>Accurate selection of study year during registration is mandatory.</li>\n<li>Participants are permitted to attempt only the rounds designated for their respective academic year.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Code of Conduct:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Registrations must be completed exclusively via the official Unstop link.</li>\n<li>One submission per individual; duplicate accounts will lead to instant ban.</li>\n<li>Strictly no use of AI tools, external assistants, or unauthorized tab-switching.</li>\n<li>Plagiarism checks will run automatically across all code submissions.</li>\n<li>The decisions made by team&nbsp;<strong>HackKro</strong>&nbsp;will be final and non-negotiable.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Judging &amp; Tie-Breaking Criteria:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>MCQ Round:</strong> Accuracy and speed (completion time)</li>\n</ul>",
